  "explanation": "Both awards are directly supported by the original sources. Document d1 explicitly states that Philip Proctor received the Austrian Decoration for Science and Art in 2001 for his work in sustainable manufacturing and renewable energy. Document d2 confirms that he received the Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire in 1923 for his contributions to New Zealand’s industrial development. These are distinct awards given to the same individual at different times and for different achievements, and neither contradicts the other."
